# ogarza.plugins.weather

Read `AGENTS.md` before non-trivial edits. Keep replies and diffs small.

- Persist via `loadPersisted` / `persistSettings` only (including `quality`, `resolution`, `detail`, `shaderDetail`, `hyprEnabled`, `overlayTarget`, and `hyprBaseDamage`). Never write `/usr/share/omarchy/` or `~/.config/hypr/`.
- Mode `none` is default (overlay off). Panel Settings is that row and does not `setMode`. Follow/Exclusive never select `fire`, `rainbow`, or `custom`.
- Follow: `locationReady` then Open-Meteo (coords) or wttr. WMO `0` is sunny (`parseWeatherCode`, not `code || ""`).
- Compositor: fade `overlayFromPreset` → `overlayToPreset`. Follow 10s, panel 2s. Mixes = two or three slots. Resolution downscales the layer stack except Native. Effect detail is shader `quality` 0–3. Target `screen` (default) or `wallpaper` (`overlayTarget`). Wallpaper uses `WlrLayer.Bottom` and **clears** Hyprland `screen_shader` immediately. Rain refraction on wallpaper is `wallpaper_warp.frag` (`docs/wallpaper-target.md`). While `hyprEnabled` on screen target, keep one Hyprland `screen_shader` (`HyprShader.js`, `tex`/`time`); rain mix 0↔1 on `time`, motion uses `TIME_OFFSET`. Skip painted rain when `hyprEnabled` and `refract` > 0 (`overlaySkipsRainDrops`). Alternate `current.a.frag` / `current.b.frag` so Hyprland reloads. Scan sibling plugin folders for `screen_shader` and warn on the panel. Overlay `*.frag.qsb` are committed; warn on the panel if a baked overlay shader is missing.
- Shaders: premultiplied `vec4(rgb * a, a) * qt_Opacity * strength`. Keep the std140 uniform block in sync. Stormy: no arrays / baked bolt tables (blank overlay); see `shaders.mdc`.
- Panel params: columns from `fieldsForVisualLayer` / `fieldsForPanel`. Settings page is Resolution + per-shader Effect detail (`settingsLodRows`, persist `shaderDetail`). Follow → live `weatherPreset`; Exclusive → `exclusivePreset`. Mixes and singles expand one column per layer (optional rainbow last). Custom: stacked A/B/C pickers (`none` is off).
- New weather types: `Model.js` modes + maps + params; `Service.qml` only if compositor/fetch changes.
- Docs: README + CHANGELOG + manifest version when behavior changes.
